            "description": "A new paranoia and fear hangs like mildew over Britain. Buoyed by the heightened fear against potential new terrorist attacks. Jack Straw and David Blunkett are in unison lobbying you to pass the Anti-Terrorism, Crime and Security Bill. A puff from your chest swells as you sense the opportunity to capitalise on an unprecedented political capital. The steely eyes of the foreign policy hawks gaze upon you, awaiting whether or not you'll give this thing the green light. The question is: will parliament, and the people?",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
