    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12841,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Only 3 days after the local elections results, the European elections are yet again a disappointment for Labour. The machine at the local level has faltered once again. Instead this time, the Conservatives didn’t make gains at all, and all of the profit went to UKIP – led by Roger Knapman. This is a formal representation, a real manifestation, of the rise of Euroscepticism.",
