    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12851,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "As you were getting ready to announce the election, the phone rings in Downing street. For a few seconds, you stand in disbelief. Pope John Paul II, holding the Papacy for more than 28 years, has died aged 84. You have to delay the election. Still reckoning with the passing, you begin to write a statement…",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12856,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Just like in 2001, 4 years prior, you have decided to make your first official speech during Prime Minister’s Questions. the Tory leader has just railed against your government's record, claiming you broke promises on taxes, immigration and university top-up fees, saying repeatedly: \"Why should anyone believe him again?\". You need to respond, for the sake of the country.",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12861,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "With the grilling of Prime Minister’s Questions at last over, you now must announce the election outside the famous large black door of No. 10. All of the cameras and journalists are locked on your face, ready to broadcast your speech. What will you centre your speech around, given that this will be the first shot of the campaign?",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12866,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Parliament is officially dissolved, and a core tenant of the electoral system must be sorted: the party manifesto. Within the little red booklet is housed all of your policy proposals and policies for the populace to eat up – or mostly the media class. Still, how the manifesto will be composited is yet to be decided. The team now needs to know how you would like to tinker this book so that it's camera ready.",
