    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12891,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "In Longbridge, the West Midlands, a dying gasp of the dwindling automobile industry has finally been choked out. Chinese-bought firm MG Rover is facing an imminent collapse, and is about to go under. Thousands of car manufacturing jobs are at risk. Action must be taken.",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12896,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Much to the vexation of both yourself, and the Tories, the Liberal Democrats are expected to perform significantly better than in prior elections. Under the leadership of Charles Kennedy, their uptick could see them breach the 20% If they perform well enough, there is even a possibility that they will contribute to a hung parliament. We can’t afford to bleed our voters. What shall we do?",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12901,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Yet another problem with the Liberal Democrats. Not only are they performing better in their own right than in previous elections, but they are sucking out a good chunk of Labour voters due to your troubling decisions in Iraq. We need to do something to keep them with us, but what?",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
