    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 12911,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "A topic that has gained momentum and importance in our politics is the issue of crime. The Conservatives have taken the attack to your government, thanks to recent reports from the British Crime Survey stating that violent crime had risen by 9% in the last 3 months of 2004 – despite the same report showing a 5% decrease in crime overall. As the incumbent party, how will you go about countering this attack?",
