        "pk": 14645,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Very rarely have you ever come face to face with Mr Howard in politics. Seeing how Tony batted off and outmanoeuvred, it makes you weary reminding yourself that he’s still their leader at all. All you have to do now is tighten your iron grip around the Tory campaign’s neck, making sure the weasel doesn’t slip through.",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 14401,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "The campaign has unfolded into a chaotic, messy affair. That escapade now, is in the past, Brown. You have many accolades with your name: the Iron Chancellor, the Progressive Centrist, the man who could finally win it to cement Labour for years to come. With you heading the party, it falls to you to finish this election campaign off. What will you do to convince the voters to back Labour at this pivotal penultimate hour?",
            "likelihood": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 14952,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "The house is divided. It's all burning to the ground.<p></p>Gordon <i>hates</i> that you stole his throne all those years ago in 1994. The apartment complexes of Downing Street insulates a mist of despair. Your Ministers whisper of the letter box filled with Labour MP's clamoring for you to resign. It all makes your blood rush around your head, haemorrhaging your skull.<p></p>Suddenly, you feel it.<p></p>Your heartbeat accelerates at break-neck speed. Then it falls off a cliff. And into the abyss.<p></p>Your mind scarpers desperately to 2003.<p></p>Not again. Not like this.",
            "likelihood": 1
