    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 14294,
        "fields": {
            "priority": 0,
            "description": "Iain Duncan Smith suffered the wrath of his parliamentary cohort, and was thrown out as your party machine continued to roll ahead. Their fatigue in the face of your increasingly stentorian liberalism, has caused them to rally around the yet-again-transformed Michael Portillo. As he fires his opening shots for the campaign, his attacks centre around your abandonment of “Middle Britain”, your neglect of the “power of enterprise and of the citizens to lift themselves up”. You’re bleeding centrist voters fast. But, he’s not invincible. Knock him down some pegs.",
